* RELEASES 


Version: 2010_v1.0.0
............................................................................................................................
This is the code which was used for the 2010a 0.323E+20 POT muon-disappearance analysis.
Details may be found in T2K-TN-36 (v4).

Version: 2010_v2.0.0 
............................................................................................................................
This is the code which was used for the 2010b 1.431E+20 POT muon-disappearance analysis.
Details may be found in T2K-TN-64 (v3).

2010_v2.1.0
............................................................................................................................
Similar to 2010_v2.0.0 but with the following change requested during the analysis review:
> The nd280 efficiency error was increased from +/-5% to +5.6% -5.2% to match the one used in the nue analysis.
> The statistical error of the ND280 CC inclusive measurement (~2.7%) was also propagated to SK.


2010_v3.0.0
............................................................................................................................
This code was used for the 2010b 1.431E+20 POT 3-flavour muon-neutrino disappearance analysis (details in T2K-TN-88)
and for the 2010b 1.431E+20 POT joint 3-flavour analysis (details in T2K-TN-131)

2012_v1.0.0
............................................................................................................................
This is the code used for the official 2012 3+E_20 POT 3-flavour muon-neutrino disappearance analysis.
A *major* re-write of the analysis wrt to the 2010 releases since the analysis inputs and
the analysis procedure (fitting for systematics) were very different.
Details, too numerous to mention here, may be found in T2K-TN-141 (v4).
This is the first freeze of the fully validated 2012 code: This branch also contains experimental and 
deprecated features (experimental FSI and BANFF binnings, systematics not used in the final analysis,
deprecated macros etc) that will be removed from a near-future "streamlined" revision.

2012_v2.0.0
............................................................................................................................
Implemented the 2012 3-flavour electron-neutrino appearance analysis and the 2012 joint 3-flavour oscillation analysis.
The source tree was cleaned-up (Experimental FSI and BANFF systematic binnings, systematics not used in the analysis 
were removed.  Deprecated data files, macros and scripts were removed.  Code experimenting with the use of principal 
components analysis in the study of the effect of systematics in the oscillation fit was deleted.)
The main Minuit and the experimental Minuit2 fit implementations were "unified" so that one can switch between the two 
transparently. A GSL fitter was implementing, adding the following fit methods in our analysis:
Simulated annealing, Levemberg-Marquardt, Fletcher-Reeves conjugate gradient, Polak-Ribiere conjugate gradient,
Vector Broyden-Fletcher-Goldfarb-Shanno (BFGS), Steepest Descent.
Significant fit CPU-efficiency improvement as the jont analysis considers ~90 systematics.

Current trunk
............................................................................................................................
2013 6E+20 POT muon-neutrino disappearance development code.


Future releases:


